# mirrors.schema — who may set each key of the `mirrors` subsystem (see w-conf.md).
# Format: <KEY>\t<scope>   scope: system | user | both
#
# There is exactly one /etc/pacman.d/mirrorlist and exactly one machine-wide
# package manager reading it, so every key here is system-scope. A per-user
# override would not be meaningless-but-harmless: it would let any account steer
# where the machine downloads its software from.
COUNTRY	system
PROTOCOL	system
AGE	system
SCORE	system
COUNT	system
THREADS	system
CONNECT_TIMEOUT	system
DOWNLOAD_TIMEOUT	system
INTERVAL_DAYS	system
SKIP_METERED	system
